```sql
BEGIN;
INSERT INTO t (a, b) VALUES (...), (...), (...);  -- bulk values
-- ... up to 500 rows per INSERT
COMMIT;
```. 1000-10000x faster than per-row commits. For huge: read file in Python + use `executemany`: `cur.executemany('INSERT ...', rows)`. Pre-create indexes AFTER bulk load (insert without index, then `CREATE INDEX`). Use `PRAGMA synchronous = OFF;` + WAL for fastest (risky — data loss on power failure).

